thinking in AB InBev, where

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:02.950
you think machine learning may
help, or already is helping?

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:04.440
ADAM SPUNBERG:
Sure and, you know,

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.100
part of that digital
transformation

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.600
I was speaking to before--

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.830
we're trying to find ways
to automate the breweries,

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.380
but in a smart way.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.180
It's not just enough to--

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.730
we're not trying to replace
people with technology.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:20.110
We're trying to find
technology that--

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:21.510
as Manju alluded to--

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:25.740
improves quality,
reduces costs, and just

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.710
makes us more efficient in
general as an operation.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:33.720
And for example, take something
like predictive maintenance,

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.460
which we're alluding to here.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.200
Say you have a machine
